<section class="fragment-plan" data-artifact="plan" data-slice="tactics-and-ai" data-rev="0">
  <!-- @include-skip the published snippets are hand-inlined here as in the sibling plans, so the five plan fragments share one markup -->
  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">data</span> content/tactics.json (new); tuning.json, rules/default.json, README.md (modified)</summary><div class="pl-card">The tactics schema: four formations, five mentalities, six instructions, roles mapped to attributes, three duties, and the AI manager's thresholds. Tuning version 2 with the decision weights, the fatigue curve, and injury rates. Rule pack version 3 with windows_exempt for half-time.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>content/</td><td>+369 / -11</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/data/tactics.rs (new); data/mod.rs, attributes.rs, rules.rs, tuning.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The fail-closed tactics loader with a cross-file role check; fourteen required attributes; the substitution exemptions; the fatigue block the engine now reads.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>crates/engine/src/data</td><td>+377 / -19</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/tactics/mod.rs, tactics/change.rs, ai.rs, fatigue.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The tactics model and a per-team plan computed once per change; the stoppage-gated change queue inside the engine with the substitution ledger and the conflict rule; the AI manager on threshold rules with no random draws; energy, the fatigue curve, and injury rolls.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>crates/engine/src</td><td>+1010</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">domain</span> crates/engine/src/decision.rs, player.rs, team.rs, sim.rs, rules/mod.rs, rules/restart.rs, tuning.rs, snapshot.rs, scenario.rs, validate.rs, lib.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The scored-options decision layer; squad identity, energy, and statuses on each player; formations and plan offsets in the anchors; changes applied on the stoppage tick; injury stoppages with a dropped ball; snapshot version 2; scene helpers; validator exemptions.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine/src</td><td>+788 / -167</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">observability</span> crates/engine/src/observe/mod.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">match-stats gains shots, injury.count, fatigue.mean_pct, the change counts, substitutions, and darkpath.change_never_applied. Shots on target stay with the statistics work that defines them.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine/src/observe</td><td>+36</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> crates/engine/tests/tactics_queue.rs, substitutions.rs, fatigue.rs, injury.rs, strength.rs, ai_trailing.rs, mentality.rs (new); common/mod.rs, content.rs, snapshot.rs, full_match.rs, validator.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">One file per criterion. The three statistical criteria are slow tests run in release across threads; the continuation test crosses a substitution and a tactics change.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>crates/engine/tests</td><td>+966 / -10</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">contract</span> crates/protocol/src/event.rs, command.rs (comment), message.rs, lib.rs; docs/reference/protocol.md</summary><div class="pl-card">Substitution, injury, and ai-decision events and the change.applied_tick and ai.decision fields, all reserved by the observability contract; team.id on change events. The queue-change detail stays opaque: its format is an open product-owner question. Protocol version 2 survives because every addition is additive.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/protocol and docs</td><td>+85 / -12</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">cli</span> crates/engine-cli/src/stream_run.rs, serve.rs, simulate.rs, resume.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">The driver maps the new events and refreshes player ids after a substitution; the AI manages the away team in serve; resume restores managers and tactics from the snapshot.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>crates/engine-cli</td><td>+59 / -10</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">ui</span> web/stoppages.mjs, tests/stoppages.test.mjs; README.md</summary><div class="pl-card">The injury event joins the list of events that stop play; the README names tactics, fatigue, injuries, substitutions, and the slow-test command.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>web/ and root</td><td>+27 / -2</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R1 · Processor time per match exceeds the 10 percent tripwire</div><div class="callout-body">Baseline 418.8 ms per match and 1.4965 microseconds per tick on 837cb5c; the limits are 460.7 ms and 6.82 MB. The plan is precomputed and the refresh and check intervals are coarse. Step 21 measures three drives; a miss goes to the product owner with the levers, and no lever is pulled silently.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R2 · The stronger team does not win more than half</div><div class="callout-body">Judged before calibration over 200 matches split home and away. Finishing, decisions, composure, and vision now reach the decision layer; a failure is fixed with the decision weights inside this slice and recorded with the counts.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R3 · A resumed match drifts after a change</div><div class="callout-body">Snapshot version 2 carries squad identity, energy, tactics, the ledger, the queue, and the AI state; the continuation test crosses a substitution and a tactics change byte for byte.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><div class="callout-hd">R4 · Play turns passive or chaotic</div><div class="callout-body">Hold carries a negative base and a held-time penalty; the possession and idle-ball bands stay in the full-match test; calibration tunes the weights.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R5 · Injury stoppages lengthen matches</div><div class="callout-body">About 0.6 injuries per match by default, each adding 60 seconds to the half; ticks per match is reported beside the gate.</div></aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><div class="callout-hd">R6 · Unrelated staged files ride into the commit</div><div class="callout-body">The index holds staged work from elsewhere; the commit names its own paths explicitly.</div></aside>
  </div>
